    "engine": "knitr",
    "markdown": "---\ntitle: \"Which Nigerian states got worse, and their deadliest months\"\ndescription: \"Thirty-three of thirty-seven states got worse between 2015 and 2025, at speeds from 1.5 to 59.8 per cent a year. Borno, one death in three, barely moved. Rank by speed and rank by size are different lists.\"\ndate: 2026-11-06\ncategories:\n  - stats-cases\nengine: knitr\ncode-fold: true\ncode-summary: \"Show the analysis\"\nimage: thumbnail.png\nimage-alt: \"Thirty-seven horizontal confidence intervals, one per state, ordered by growth rate. Most point right of zero; four straddle it. Borno sits near the bottom, almost flat.\"\n---\n\n## Question\n\n\"Nigeria is getting worse\" is one number, and nothing in it says where. Which states got worse, and which months were deadliest?\n\n## Claim\n\nThe headline is true. 29,300 events and 94,586 deaths, 2015 to 2025 (data). A national rate of +22.9 per cent a year (model).\n\nIt is also the least useful number in the file.\n\n## Counter-claim\n\nTwo facts a national average cannot carry.\n\nThe state with the most deaths is not the state worsening fastest (model). And a deadlier month is not a busier one (data).\n\n## Setup\n\nOne row per state, LGA, year and month: 772 cells, 37 states, 2015 to 2026 (data). The analysis fits 2015 to 2025. 2026 is six months and still being revised, so it sits out.\n\nEvery number is tagged: **(data)** counted in the file, **(model)** fitted, **(proof)** arithmetic.\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n\n```{.r .cell-code}\nsource(\"analysis.R\")\n\npal <- c(worse = \"#0f766e\", flat = \"#6b7280\", deaths = \"#b45309\",\n         events = \"#0e7490\", ink = \"#57606a\")\ngrid <- \"#d7dce1\"\n```\n:::\n\n\n## The analysis\n\n### Thirty-seven speeds, one direction\n\nThe national rate is the middle of a wide spread. State trends run from +1.5 to +59.8 per cent a year (model), a standard deviation of 14.5 points (model). Thirty-three states are worse than flat. Four are flat, and none improves (model).\n\nSokoto leads at +59.8 per cent (model). Its toll in eleven years is 2,372 deaths (data). Borno's is 35,355 (data).\n\n\n::: {.cell}\n::: {#fig-trend .cell-output-display}\n\n```{=html}\n<div id=\"htmlwidget-50f4aa15e88d662c9f56\" style=\"width:100%;height:619px;\" class=\"plotly html-widget\"></div>\n<script type=\"application/json\" data-for=\"htmlwidget-50f4aa15e88d662c9f56\">{\"x\":{\"visdat\":{\"198051c056b9\":[\"function () \",\"plotlyVisDat\"]},\"cur_data\":\"198051c056b9\",\"attrs\":{\"198051c056b9\":{\"x\":{},\"y\":{},\"mode\":\"markers\",\"marker\":{\"color\":{},\"size\":7},\"error_x\":{\"type\":\"data\",\"symmetric\":false,\"array\":{},\"arrayminus\":{},\"color\":\"#9aa4b2\",\"thickness\":1.1000000000000001,\"width\":0},\"hovertemplate\":\"%{y}: %{x:.1f}% a year<extra><\\/extra>\",\"alpha_stroke\":1,\"sizes\":[10,100],\"spans\":[1,20],\"type\":\"scatter\"}},\"layout\":{\"height\":640,\"margin\":{\"b\":10,\"l\":10,\"t\":30,\"r\":60},\"showlegend\":false,\"shapes\":[{\"type\":\"line\",\"yref\":\"paper\",\"y0\":0,\"y1\":1,\"x0\":22.945323953401097,\"x1\":22.945323953401097,\"line\":{\"color\":\"#57606a\",\"width\":1,\"dash\":\"dot\"}}],\"annotations\":[{\"x\":22.945323953401097,\"yref\":\"paper\",\"y\":1,\"xanchor\":\"center\",\"yanchor\":\"bottom\",\"showarrow\":false,\"text\":\"country: +22.9\",\"font\":{\"size\":12,\"color\":\"#57606a\"}},{\"x\":8.9018325687151734,\"y\":\"Borno\",\"xanchor\":\"left\",\"yanchor\":\"bottom\",\"showarrow\":false,\"xshift\":8,\"text\":\"Borno\",\"font\":{\"size\":12,\"color\":\"#b45309\"}},{\"x\":59.819407658412338,\"y\":\"Sokoto\",\"xanchor\":\"right\",\"yanchor\":\"bottom\",\"showarrow\":false,\"xshift\":-8,\"text\":\"Sokoto\",\"font\":{\"size\":12,\"color\":\"#b45309\"}}],\"xaxis\":{\"domain\":[0,1],\"automargin\":true,\"title\":\"events per year, 2015-2025 (% change a year)\",\"gridcolor\":\"#d7dce1\",\"zeroline\":false,\"tickfont\":{\"size\":12}},\"yaxis\":{\"domain\":[0,1],\"automargin\":true,\"title\":\"\",\"tickfont\